From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfplat: media buffer wrapper, bitmap image size, FP16 arrays, legacy buffer offset, Copy2DTo, file byte stream SetLength/Flush/Close, byte stream on IStream

Stubs, as documented now:

- MFCreateMediaBufferWrapper ("@ stub"): a media buffer over a byte range
  of another one (offset, length checked against the original's maximum,
  E_INVALIDARG otherwise); Lock returns the range, SetCurrentLength is
  bounded by the range, the original's length is untouched.
- MFCreateLegacyMediaBufferOnMFMediaBuffer with an offset (was E_NOTIMPL):
  the legacy buffer is the rest of the media buffer after the offset.
- MFCalculateBitmapImageSize ("@ stub"): rows of RGB/bitfield formats are
  padded to 32 bits, known YUV FOURCCs use MFCalculateImageSize, any other
  format reports biSizeImage with known = FALSE.
- MFConvertToFP16Array / MFConvertFromFP16Array ("@ stub"): IEEE half
  precision, round to nearest even, subnormals, infinity and NaN.
- IMF2DBuffer2::Copy2DTo (E_NOTIMPL): copies the planes into the
  destination, MF_E_BUFFERTOOSMALL when it is smaller.
- The 2D buffers' IMFGetService: MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE for a service
  they do not offer (E_NOTIMPL before); same for the file byte stream.
- File byte stream SetLength (SetEndOfFile), Flush (FlushFileBuffers for
  writable streams) and Close (releases the file handle).
- MFCreateMFByteStreamOnStreamEx: wraps an IStream; anything else is
  E_INVALIDARG (there is no WinRT stream here).
- The property store's Commit is S_OK (the values live in memory).

---
